scratch/

# 2026-08-27 (Wave J1). Figures referenced by README.md and docs/. `*.png` (line 25)
# ignores them, so Wave I had to `git add -f` them. Naming them here removes the
# need for `-f`: a regenerated figure can be staged the ordinary way, and anyone
# who deletes and re-renders one does not have to know about the force flag.
#
# CORRECTION to what this comment said in an earlier draft: it claimed the `-f`
# route "leaves a REGENERATED figure invisible to `git status`". That is FALSE and
# was asserted without testing. .gitignore has no effect on files that are already
# tracked, so a modified tracked PNG shows up either way. Verified 2026-08-27 by
# removing these three lines and re-testing: the modified file still reported `AM`.
# What the negation actually changes is only `git check-ignore --no-index`, i.e.
# whether an UNTRACKED copy of the path can be added without `-f`. Keeping the
# lines for that reason; deleting the false justification.
!docs/assets/report_intervention_waterfall.png
!docs/assets/report_comparison_intervention_waterfall.png
!docs/assets/report_compound_confidence_overlay.png
# Wave S3 evidence artifacts (2026-08-27): the first rate-level calibration of the sugar
# trunk, and its score against the pre-registered hold-out.
#
# `trunk_rate_calibration_refit.{json,md}` MUST be tracked, and not only for review. It is
# the machine-readable declaration of a FIT CORPUS: `scripts/ci/fit_target_gate.py` and
# `src/fit_target_index.py` read its `fit_target_files` and `fit_leverage` blocks, and
# `scripts/ci/holdout_guard.py` check 4 scans it (the `refit` in the filename is what puts
# it in that scan). Untracked, CI would run with the fit undeclared and unguarded, which is
# the exact failure mode the fit-target gate exists to prevent. It is also cited by name
# from the headers of src/barrier_constants.py and data/lit/arrhenius_params.yml, where it
# is the evidence for the Schiff/Amadori ordering resolution.
!results/validation/trunk_rate_calibration_refit.json
!results/validation/trunk_rate_calibration_refit.md
# The pre/post score against the frozen pre-registration. Tracked because a wave that
# reports "the hold-out did not move" has to leave behind the artifact that shows it did
# not, target by target, rather than a sentence saying so. Append-only companion to
# maillard_path_holdout_frozen_predictions.*, which it reads and never regenerates.
!results/validation/maillard_path_holdout_S3_prepost.json
!results/validation/maillard_path_holdout_S3_prepost.md

# Wave X evidence artifact (2026-08-28): the norfuraneol barrier fit against Hofmann &
# Schieberle 1998 Table 4. Tracked for three reasons, each sufficient on its own.
# (1) `scripts/ci/fit_target_gate.py` and `src/fit_target_index.py` scan
#     results/validation/*refit*.json as FIT RECORDS; this is the file that declares
#     `hofmann1998_norfuraneol_h2s_145C_20min_pH5` a fit target, and an untracked
#     declaration would let a scored panel row quietly double as a fit target on any
#     machine that had not run the generator.
# (2) The fit was REJECTED by its own pre-registered isotope gate, so the record is the
#     only place the REASON the shipped barrier is still its unfitted class seed exists.
#     A rejected fit that leaves no artifact is indistinguishable from a fit never run.
# (3) tests/scientific/test_wave_x_step_level_2026_08.py reads it and asserts that the
#     shipped constant, the gate's verdict and the test's own ceiling all agree.
!results/validation/furanone_reductive_sulfhydrylation_refit_hofmann.json
!results/validation/furanone_reductive_sulfhydrylation_refit_hofmann.md

# Wave Y evidence artifacts (2026-08-28): the volatile-budget / marker-yield workstream.
# Five files, tracked for five distinct reasons; none is a convenience copy.
#
# (1) The marker-yield re-derivation is a FIT RECORD. `scripts/ci/fit_target_gate.py`,
#     `src/fit_target_index.py` and `holdout_guard` check 4 all scan
#     results/validation/*rederivation*.json, and this is the file that declares the two
#     Pratap-Singh benchmarks and Trikusuma as targets of the relocated shared scale.
#     Untracked, CI would run with the relocation undeclared and unguarded.
!results/validation/matrix_marker_yield_rederivation.json
!results/validation/matrix_marker_yield_rederivation.md
# (2) The projection-budget constraint record. Its filename must NEVER contain `refit` or
#     `rederivation`: nothing was fitted from it, no constant moved, and the two gates would
#     otherwise treat the step-level rows it scores as fit targets and strip them from
#     scored evidence -- which would delete the very rows that constrain the budget. It is
#     tracked because the DECISION not to apply the constraint is only defensible with the
#     measured counterfactual beside it.
!results/validation/projection_budget_step_yield_constraint.json
!results/validation/projection_budget_step_yield_constraint.md
# (3) The pre-registration. Written before any constant was edited and before anything was
#     re-scored, including the one amendment (change 2 withdrawn) and its reason. A wave
#     that scores itself against predictions it wrote afterwards has proved nothing; this
#     file is what makes the scoring in the ledger checkable.
!results/validation/wave_y_prereg_predictions.json
# (4) The pre/post against the frozen maillard_path hold-out. Same rule as the Wave S3
#     companion, plus one this wave added: it carries the ABLATION that attributes the 8
#     drifted targets to Wave X's norfuraneol channel rather than to this wave, and an
#     attribution claim with no artifact behind it is an assertion.
!results/validation/maillard_path_holdout_wave_y_prepost.json
!results/validation/maillard_path_holdout_wave_y_prepost.md
# (5) The barrier-sensitivity decomposition (on a Wave Z1 lead). It reproduces Wave Z1's
#     1.22x, splits the ~13x deficit into span saturation and allocation normalisation, and
#     measures that the budget constants CANNOT restore sensitivity. Nothing is fitted; the
#     filename deliberately avoids `refit`/`rederivation` for the same reason as (2).
!results/validation/barrier_sensitivity_deficit.json
!results/validation/barrier_sensitivity_deficit.md

# Wave R1 evidence artifact (2026-08-28): both frozen hold-outs scored BEFORE and AFTER the
# retirement of the auto-accepted barrier offsets. Tracked because it is the only place the
# price of honesty is written down: the retired model is ~8% WORSE on the median fold error
# of the maillard_path pre-registration (10.05x -> 10.86x), and the eight-point matrix
# hold-out cannot see the change at all. A README that claims "the honest numbers are worse"
# owes the reader the file that measures it. Nothing here is fitted and no hold-out was
# regenerated or re-frozen -- the frozen pre-registration is READ; the "before" arm is
# reconstructed through the BARRIER_OFFSETS environment variable in a subprocess. The
# filename deliberately avoids `refit`/`rederivation` so that fit_target_gate and
# holdout_guard do not mistake a hold-out SCORECARD for a fit record.
!results/validation/holdout_prepost_barrier_offset_retirement.json
!results/validation/holdout_prepost_barrier_offset_retirement.md
